{{begin-newsitem |time=2026-09-20T12:48:30Z |title=BlizzCon 2026 |author=Ojan |resources=sc-trailer-holt.png |categories=StarCraft, WarCraft III |summary=BlizzCon 2026 announcements}}

I am probably the last person interested in Blizzard games to hear this, but BlizzCon 2026 wrapped up a week ago. It was last held in 2023, so it's been a while.

There are some announcements for the Warcraft and StarCraft franchises:

- Warcraft III gets its first new campaign in over 20 years: "Return to the Last Days of Lordaeron to experience the fall of one great city and play a part in the founding of another". Blizzard released a [Launch Trailer](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=I1kXClUCyuA), which seems pretty close to the original intro of Warcraft III from back in the days: two armies clash in futile strife, as the real threat appears from above. A gameplay trailer can be seen [here](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=m-C20pyrvjk). It is already available from [Blizzard](https://blizzard.com).

- Blizzard is working on a new StarCraft game! It is an open world, first person shooter that is apparently single player and character focused. The [Announce Cinematic](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=9eQUtOQXYgQ) is pretty gorgeous, but there seems to be no gameplay footage available, and the game is set to be released in 2030; offering "plenty of time for delays". For a deeper dive into what the game might be like, I enjoyed [GameDad VII](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=q0i6hBYgHmc)'s analysis.

{{img |file=sc-trailer-holt.png |title=Still from the StarCraft trailer}}

For me, it certainly sparks excitement to experience the StarCraft universe from this angle. Of course, Warcraft III from 2002 and the new upcomming StarCraft game of 2030 are both much to new for this site; {{highlight |text=Jorvik Systems}} is dedicated to Warcraft I, Warcraft II and StarCraft from the good ole nineties so don't expect much coverage on this site {{dash}} but it's not every day that 23 year old games get a new campaign and the StarCraft universe expand into new types of games.
